The '''Capture Pennant Spell''' is a niche-spell used in the [[Silver-White Capture Pennant]].

==Description==
While the image quality for this spell is poor, it appears as if it has a central square shaped sigil with what may be a diamond inside, somewhat similar to a light spell, surrounded by signs similar in appearance to the footprint of a chicken (with a shorter back toe) pointing away from the center, and a sign similar to an arrow with a filled-in tip pointing towards the center. The spell is believed to allow the capture pennants of the [[Knights Moralis]] to be controlled by the person using the spell, allowing them to wrap the banner around people and objects. However, as a spell similar to a [[Repetition Seal|repetition seal]] was also seen on one of the banners earlier in the story,{{Ref|m|12}} it is unknown which spell actually lets the banner be controlled, or if it's both of them working in tandem.

==Usage==
The spell, while only directly seen on the cover [[Volume 9|volume 9]], is used each time the [[Knights Moralis]] use their capture pennants, the contraption this spell is part of. These pennants are used by the knights to hold people (typically criminals{{Ref|m|49}} or injured persons{{Ref|m|12}}) or objects in place by wrapping them securely in the fabric of the banner, and even aid in moving people or items from place to place.

